  "narrative": "No new validation was released for this synthesis; the only independent validation available remains the validation of H7. Therefore, the currently strongest evidence in the supplied lung-cell-line dataset consists of four very large dataset-level associations, each far exceeding any plausible 10% relative-difference benchmark on the dependency-score scale. Because many dependency scores have negative means, I judged the clinical-significance threshold primarily against the scale and standard deviation of the dependency scores rather than as a literal percent change in a negative quantity; all accepted effects are around 0.75 to 0.85, i.e. several standard deviations.\n\nThe accepted associations are: H6, TP53-wild-type cells have much stronger USP7 dependency than TP53-loss cells; H7, SMARCA4-loss cells have much stronger SMARCA2 dependency than SMARCA4-intact cells, and this claim is independently validated by R13; H9, MSI-high cells have much stronger WRN dependency than MSI-low cells; and H13, KEAP1-loss cells have weaker NFE2L2 dependency, i.e. a less negative/higher dependency_NFE2L2 score, than KEAP1-intact cells. H13 is the reversed, biologically counterintuitive version of the original H10 formulation, and H10 was correctly rejected as directionally wrong.\n\nThe robustness follow-ups materially strengthen the accepted effects but do not establish causality or external generalizability. The SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 association is present both when ARID1A is lost and when it is intact, with estimates +0.814 and +0.777, respectively, and the ARID1A-by-SMARCA4 interaction is small and crosses zero, so there is no reliable evidence that ARID1A loss modifies the main association. The SMARCA4 effect is also retained in the KY-library subset. The USP7/TP53 wild-type association is retained within MYC-amplified cells and within the KY-library subset. The WRN/MSI-high association is retained in adenocarcinoma and after restricting the comparator to cells with mutation burden of at least four, although H17 is not a true interaction test because the exposed MSI-high set is largely unchanged. The KEAP1/NFE2L2 association is retained in the KY-library subset and among STK11-wild-type cells, and the KEAP1-by-TP53-loss interaction is small and crosses zero. Thus, within this dataset, the four accepted associations are robust to the measured contexts tested so far.\n\nThe negative and null findings are also now more interpretable. Same-target associations were not supported for KRAS mutation versus KRAS dependency, BRAF V600E versus BRAF dependency, ERBB2 amplification versus ERBB2 dependency, PIK3CA mutation versus STAT3 dependency, or MYC amplification versus POLR2A dependency. Overall TP53 status did not predict MDM2 dependency. ARID1A loss alone did not predict SMARCA2 dependency. The KRAS-wild-type EGFR follow-up was small and compatible with no effect, although the original overall EGFR amplification claim remains unresolved because the initial estimate was borderline and its interval included zero. No reliable interaction evidence was found for ARID1A modifying the SMARCA4-loss effect or TP53-loss modifying the KEAP1/NFE2L2 effect.\n\nThe next most informative step is to test the unresolved claims and broaden coverage of the untested dependency outcomes. I request that the next appraise cycle prioritize independent validation of H13, because it is large but directionally unexpected and therefore has the highest value from an independent replication. If H13 validates well, H9 and H6 would also be strong validation candidates. The discovery queue should include H26 through H32 and H34 through H39, plus the newly registered RIT1/KRAS redundancy hypothesis: KRAS mutation may make RIT1 less essential because KRAS-mutant cells have constitutive MAPK-pathway activation, so direction +1 encodes a weaker RIT1 dependency/higher score. Direct-target refinements for BRAF, EGFR, or ERBB2 in mutually exclusive oncogenic contexts may be useful later, but the current priority is to fill untested outcomes and obtain validation for the main accepted effects. All conclusions remain associations within the supplied lung-cell-line dataset; causal direction, clinical biomarker status, and generalizability remain unestablished.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted dataset-level effects: H6 TP53 WT stronger USP7; H7 SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2 and independently validated; H9 MSI-high stronger WRN; H13 KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2/higher score. Rejected original H10 due reversed direction. Robustness accepted and closed: H14-H15 SMARCA4 effect present with/without ARID1A loss, H16 no ARID1A interaction; H17 WRN effect retained with higher-TMB comparator; H18 USP7 effect retained in MYC-amplified; H21 USP7 effect retained KY; H22 NFE2L2 effect retained KY; H23 SMARCA4 effect retained KY; H25 no KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction; H31 NFE2L2 effect retained STK11 WT; H33 WRN effect retained adenocarcinoma. Negative/closed: H1 KRAS, H2 BRAF, H4 ERBB2, H5 MDM2 TP53, H8 ARID1A/SMARCA2, H10 original KEAP1 direction, H11 PIK3CA/STAT3, H12 MYC/POLR2A, H16, H19 EGFR KRAS WT, H25. Unresolved: H3 EGFR overall; H24 EGFR KY; H20 WRN KY deferred due possible sparse cells; new queue H26-H30, H32, H34-H39, H40 RIT1/kras. Next priorities: in appraise request independent validation of H13 first; then H9/H6 if warranted. Run H26-H39 and H40 to cover untested outcomes/subtypes. Later consider conditional direct-target refinements if EGFR remains ambiguous."
